From 9b0448905f6923bb9201ff3ac2f946fc90db9d68 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Senior Matthew <SeniorMatt@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 14:25:08 +0500
Subject: [PATCH 14/24] kcm_users: accounts and fingerprint device read
 asynchronously, avatar scan on first use

Page type: List with a per-user Form page (docs/page-design.md section 1, Device-like). The existing two-pane layout
(users list in the sidebar, selected user's Form page next to it via kcm.push) already has this shape and is kept; no control
moved or was renamed. All AccountsService / fprintd calls, polkit use (nothing new on open), apply jobs and the wallet code are
unchanged. NOT BUILT YET (owner stopped heavy work); checked statically only.

Structure: unchanged. Added: busy indicator only after 150 ms; the user page is pushed when the accounts are loaded.
Relabel table: inventory/relabel/kcm_users.tsv (outer repo). Full inventory check: LOST 0 (the per-KCM --strict run reports
the same plugin/dialog rows as before this commit, 22 -> 21, since wording is unchanged and only two markers were added).
HIG ids: HIG-001, HIG-006; page-design sections 4, 7.

Speed (cause found in code, not measured). Everything below ran in the KCM constructor or the first user setPath, blocking:
- UserModel: ListCachedUsers() + reply.waitForFinished() (system bus; wakes accounts-daemon if idle), then per user
  User::setPath(): systemAccount() plus loadData() = about 13 blocking property reads (uid, userName, iconFile, realName,
  email, accountType, each read twice in the compare-then-assign code), plus a KDisplayManager::localSessions() call.
  Now: ListCachedUsers via QDBusPendingCallWatcher; each User::setPathAsync() does ONE asynchronous
  org.freedesktop.DBus.Properties.GetAll("org.freedesktop.Accounts.User") (the Properties proxy already generated for
  fprintd) and applies the values with the same compare-and-emit code (Properties struct / applyProperties); the model fills in
  one reset when the last user is ready (new property UserModel.loaded). UserAdded users that arrive meanwhile are kept.
  loadData() (on the Changed signal) now makes one read per property instead of two. System-account users are still skipped
  like before (empty data).
- FingerprintModel: GetDefaultDevice() + waitForFinished() in the constructor (can activate fprintd). Now asynchronous;
  deviceFound() turns true when the reply arrives (devicesFoundChanged, which the button's `visible` already follows);
  scanType is now NOTIFY scanTypeChanged instead of CONSTANT because the device appears later.
- KCMUser constructor: recursive QDirIterator over every plasma/avatars dir; now done on first read of kcm.avatarFiles (only
  PicturesSheet.qml, which is itself created on demand).
- main.qml pushes UserDetailsPage when userModel.loaded, not in Component.onCompleted.
- After numbers: pending, manager will measure.

Not built yet; uncertain: connect(..., Qt::SingleShotConnection) with the 5-argument functor overload (Qt 6.0+, should be ok);
`QDBusPendingReply<QList<QDBusObjectPath>>` for ListCachedUsers (the generated proxy's type, unverified); KDisplayManager
::localSessions() is still one blocking call per user (not changed); QML users of getCurrentUser() before the model is
loaded get nullptr (only main.qml did, now gated); UserDetailsPage was not read in full.

